In practice, the conditional expectation in 𝒯i\mathcal{T}\_{i} is analytically intractable, especially under high-dimensional and path-dependent settings. To address this issue, we introduce a parametric neural network V^i​(⋅;θi)\widehat{V}\_{i}(\cdot;\theta\_{i}) at each time step tit\_{i}, whose parameters θi\theta\_{i} are estimated via least-squares regression based on simulated paths. The approximate value function V^i\widehat{V}\_{i} can be interpreted as a realization of the nonlinear operator 𝒯i\mathcal{T}\_{i} within a restricted function class, transforming the original path-dependent problem into a sequence of supervised learning tasks.

